<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50821" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vīcānus</span></b>  (post-class. collat.
		form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vī-cānĕus</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Cod.
				Just. 11, 56</span></i>), a, um, adj.
		vicus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>dwelling in a village.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tmolites ille vicanus,</span>”
				<i>villager</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Fl. 3, 8</span></i>
			: haruspices, <i>who go about from village to
				village</i>, Enn. ap. <i><span class="en">Cic. Div.
				1, 58, 132</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vīcāni</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <i>villagers</i>, <i>peasants</i>, <i>rustics</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 38, 30, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cod.
					Just. 11, 56</span></i>.</div>
